cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software (this record) and the associated article."
title: "TSO500 ctDNA tissue-of-origin analysis code (SHAPE and multimodal tissue-of-origin classification)"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-14"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jaeryuk/tso500-ctdna-too"
url: "https://github.com/jaeryuk/tso500-ctdna-too"
license-url: "https://github.com/jaeryuk/tso500-ctdna-too/blob/main/LICENSE"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code for extracting Site-directed High-resolution Analysis of Positional Endpoints
  and Entropy (SHAPE) features at transcription factor binding sites, together with all-exon
  depth, exon 1 fragment-length entropy, broad copy-number, and somatic mutation modules, and
  the late-fusion ensemble used for multimodal tissue-of-origin prediction from routine targeted
  circulating tumor DNA (TruSight Oncology 500) sequencing. Patent pending; released under a
  proprietary license for academic verification and reproducibility (see LICENSE).
keywords:
  - cell-free DNA
  - circulating tumor DNA
  - fragmentomics
  - transcription factor binding sites
  - tissue of origin
  - targeted sequencing
  - nucleosome positioning
  - machine learning
  - liquid biopsy
  - cancer of unknown primary
